      "message": "The [style guide](https://google.github.io/styleguide/cppguide.html#Inheritance) writes\n\n\u003e **Do not use `virtual` when declaring an override.** Rationale: A function or destructor marked override or final that is not an override of a base class virtual function will not compile, and this helps catch common errors. The specifiers serve as documentation; if no specifier is present, the reader has to check all ancestors of the class in question to determine if the function or destructor is virtual or not.\n\nSame issue for `process` below.",
